<PageTitle>Drawer — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Drawer</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    Structurally a <a href="/components/sheet">Sheet</a>. What vaul adds — and the only reason it
    exists — is that you can drag it shut, which on a phone is the gesture people try before they
    look for a close button. Past a third of the panel it closes; short of that it springs back.
</p>
<p class="doc-note">
    No snap points, no non-modal mode and no nesting: a <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> opened with
    <code>showModal()</code> is modal by definition, and the top layer holds one at a time. Each of
    those is listed in <code>tools/check_sections.py</code> with the reason.
</p>

